in button 91 3F modifier name=shift deck=2

# ---- mixer and browse -----------------------------------------------------------
in abs14  B6 1F 3F crossfader                  # 0 at the left
in abs14  B6 0C 2C head_mix
# MASTER LEVEL (B6 08/28) and HEADPHONE LEVEL (B6 0D/2D) send 14-bit MIDI (confirmed in the list), but the
# list does not say whether the unit also applies them in hardware. Left unmapped to avoid applying
# them twice; if those knobs do nothing, uncomment the two lines below.
# in abs14 B6 08 28 master_level
# in abs14 B6 0D 2D head_level
in rel2   B6 40 browse
in rel2   B6 64 browse scale=10                # SHIFT + turn
in button 96 41 browse_press

# ---- beat FX section (one set, on the master bus, effect slot 1) ----
# FX SELECT / SHIFT+FX SELECT: next / previous effect. BEAT arrows: shorter / longer time.
# LEVEL/DEPTH is 14-bit. The list gives status B4 for it while its channel column says 6 (B5 would be
# expected); the status column is used here, see docs/TESTING-FLX4.md.
# FX ON/OFF sends 94 47 for CH1 and CH1&CH2, 95 47 for CH2, so both toggle the master slot.
# LED for FX ON/OFF: a footnote says it blinks on NOTE ON and lights on NOTE OFF, but the message table
# lists no output message for it, so no out rule yet.
in button 94 63 fx_select unit=master slot=1 dir=1
in button 94 64 fx_select unit=master slot=1 dir=-1   # SHIFT + FX SELECT
in button 94 4A fx_time unit=master slot=1 dir=-1
in button 94 4B fx_time unit=master slot=1 dir=1
in abs14  B4 02 22 fx_wet unit=master slot=1
in button 94 47 fx_on unit=master slot=1
in button 95 47 fx_on unit=master slot=1

# ---- SMART CFX button (96 00, SHIFT 96 08): steps the colour effect the CFX knobs drive, both decks ----
# (the list names only the button; this meaning is a choice. No LED state exists for it, so its
# output message 96 00 is not driven.)
in button 96 00 color_fx deck=1 dir=1
in button 96 00 color_fx deck=2 dir=1
in button 96 08 color_fx deck=1 dir=-1
in button 96 08 color_fx deck=2 dir=-1
